Z||000008||Fiero5||05-04-2001||03:17 PM||||It's the very rare teleportation option. The rarest Fiero option of them all. I pulled this out of the Chiltons quantum mechanics Fiero manual:<P>"In conventional facsimile transmission, the original is scanned thru a modified vacuum canister on the Fiero so equiped , extracting information about it, but remains intact after the scanning process. The scanned information is sent to the receiving data chip, where it is imprinted digitally to produce a copy of the original. In quantum teleportation two objects B and C are first brought into contact and then separated. Object B is taken to the sending station, while object C is taken to the receiving station. At the sending station object B is scanned together with the original object A which one wishes to teleport, yielding some information and totally disrupting the state of A and B. The scanned information is sent to the receiving station, where it is used to select one of several treatments to be applied to object C, thereby putting C into an exact replica of the former state of A."<P>I think Archie covers this in a video? Maybe not.<P>Steve||||reg||3
